# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: deferred-probe-scripts-host-mock -- probe scripts' clautolisp backend passes --host mock, which alfe rejects
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P4
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-22

* Symptom

Found while checking encoding-probe-artifacts-and-macos-forward
(2026-10-22): every scripts/run-*-probe.{sh,ps1} and
run-encoding-experiment.{sh,ps1} builds its clautolisp backend arguments as
=--clautolisp --host mock=, and alfe now answers

: alfe: --host: Unknown --host "mock" (expected cador, cadtui, nihil)

so a clautolisp run of these scripts produces an empty report (only the
headers). The CAD backends are unaffected; no CI job runs the clautolisp
backend of these scripts (=grep -rl '"--host" "mock"' scripts= lists them).

* Proposal

Use =--host nihil= (or drop --host when the default fits) in those scripts,
then check one clautolisp run per script locally.
